# Security

bomward is static. SBOM files are hostile.

- No network access, no execution of foreign code, no shell calls.
- Enforce the input limits in ADR 0006. Reject over-limit input with an error, do not crash.
- Read only paths the user passed on the command line. Never build a path from SBOM contents.
- Never write raw SBOM strings into Markdown or terminal output. Escape them. Drop or escape control characters, including ANSI escapes.
- Do not add real malware or malicious packages as fixtures. Generate inert test data.

```rust
// Bad: a component name can inject a Markdown link or a terminal escape.
writeln!(out, "added {name}")?;

// Good: escape before the string reaches the report.
writeln!(out, "added {}", escape_markdown(name))?;
```
